{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion","id":1397652,"title":"Why the Lunars didn't take over the Realm after the Contagion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-20T04:12:42-07:00","id":1397652,"title":"Why the Lunars didn't take over the Realm after the Contagion?","content":"They have opportunity aplenty before the Empress consolidates power and resumes Dragonblooded breeding program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:19:31-07:00","id":1397655,"title":"","content":"The Sword of Creation exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:22:21-07:00","id":1397656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397655#post1397655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sword of Creation exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infiltration is always an option. And it is what Lunars do best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:24:41-07:00","id":1397657,"title":"","content":"The Lunars took just as heavy casualties in the Wyld Invasion as the Dragon Blooded. The ones strong enough to attempt any such takeover, even by stealth, were too few and scattered to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:26:30-07:00","id":1397658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion#post1397652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They have opportunity aplenty before the Empress consolidates power and resumes Dragonblooded breeding program.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Exalted were equally hard hit by the Great Contagion and the subsequent Wyld Invasion (I got the impression that nothing short of Solar medicine was really effective against it). So, its a bunch of low Essence newly Exalted Lunars vs, granted, a much reduced Dragonblooded Host and <i><b>all the frickin Sidereal Bronze Faction Ninjas who weren't around to get punked</b></i>.<br /> <br /> That would be enough to give an Elder pause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:27:36-07:00","id":1397660,"title":"","content":"Because the ones that were not killed outright are scattered, their resources are shot to hell and they are severely lacking in intelligence in what the situation is.<br /> <br /> And yes, the revival of the Sword of Creation should give one pause. And if any do turn up with murderous intent, they might just notice that Chejop Kejak is standing right there. He probably has backup, do you?<br /> <br /> Besides, at that time somebody maybe possibly has the capabilities to kill off the nascent Empress, but they're <i>far</i> from capable of taking over the Realm. They're still greatly outnumbered by a hostile Dragon Blooded host, many of whom are still sitting on impressive resources. What, do you go in, occupy a capital site and then they all just submit to you? This isn't working on Klingon or Advance Wars rules. You take out the head, the body is just going to slap you around until you run off and then they'll grow a new one.<br /> <br /> (There is no Dragon Blooded breeding program, there's just... Dragon Blooded having children with one another)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:34:59-07:00","id":1397661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397660#post1397660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, at that time somebody maybe possibly has the capabilities to kill off the nascent Empress, but they're <i>far</i> from capable of taking over the Realm. They're still greatly outnumbered by a hostile Dragon Blooded host, many of whom are still sitting on impressive resources. What, do you go in, occupy a capital site and then they all just submit to you? This isn't working on Klingon or Advance Wars rules. You take out the head, the body is just going to slap you around until you run off and then they'll grow a new one.<br /> <br /> (There is no Dragon Blooded breeding program, there's just... Dragon Blooded having children with one another)</div> </div> </div> </div>Coordinated Lunar assault can easily break such opposition and occupy the ground. Though admittedly Bronze Faction intervention remains a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:36:36-07:00","id":1397663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397655#post1397655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sword of Creation exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sword of Creation: *Exists*<br /> The Silver Pact: Am I a joke to you?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> The Fair Folk invaded from the Threshold, with what was left of the Shogunate protecting the Isle. They got mauled worse than the Deebs.<br /> <br /> As for infiltration... what do you think they've been trying to do for the past 700 years?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:41:22-07:00","id":1397664,"title":"","content":"How long did it take the Lunars to find out who fired the Sword anyway? I can imagine some probably thought at first it was a sign the Solars were back (after all, the ones familiar with what it was would know there were built in failsafes to restrict who could normally operate it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:48:53-07:00","id":1397667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397661#post1397661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coordinated Lunar assault can easily break such opposition and occupy the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does the picture of the world in the aftermath of the Balorian Crusade give you an impression that the Silver Pact could be particularly well coordinated?<br /> <br /> Many are dead, many of the living ones have been severely traumatised, they're scattered all over with ruined dominions and they don't know what went on to save the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T04:57:49-07:00","id":1397671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397667#post1397667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the picture of the world in the aftermath of the Balorian Crusade give you an impression that the Silver Pact could be particularly well coordinated?<br /> <br /> Many are dead, many of the living ones have been severely traumatised, they're scattered all over with ruined dominions and they don't know what went on to save the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>A circle of Lunar Elders and accompanying forces will be sufficient to tear apart nascent Realm. Remember, the Seven Tigers and his ilk posed existential threat to the Realm back then. They didn't command particularly impressive resource. A score of DG warlords at most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 06-20-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:04:27-07:00","id":1397673,"title":"","content":"Remember what happened to the Seven Tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:06:53-07:00","id":1397674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397673#post1397673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember what happened to the Seven Tigers.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was nuked by the Defense Grid. I don't think the Empress can get rid of a circle of Elders at once. Lunars aren't the kinds of opponents that precision strike is a viable option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:07:41-07:00","id":1397675,"title":"","content":"Also, if the Balorian Crusade is only just over, do you even want to topple the Empire that is wielding the Sword of Creation? If you're not sure you can take it intact, you might just want the Realm Defense Grid intact to scare away further Fair Folk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:10:36-07:00","id":1397677,"title":"","content":"What do you want, Numinous? Do you want answers that are consistent with the written setting, or do you want to outsmart it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:14:46-07:00","id":1397680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397677#post1397677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you want, Numinous? Do you want answers that are consistent with the written setting, or do you want to outsmart it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply can't comprehend that why none of surviving Lunar staged a takeover like Seven Tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:14:46-07:00","id":1397681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397677#post1397677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you want, Numinous? Do you want answers that are consistent with the written setting, or do you want to outsmart it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply can't comprehend that why none of surviving Lunar attempted a takeover like Seven Tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:19:44-07:00","id":1397683,"title":"","content":"But you've got like 6 proper answers to that by now, what else is there?<br /> They probably couldn't, and might not have wanted to is what it boils down to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:35:50-07:00","id":1397690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397683#post1397683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you've got like 6 proper answers to that by now, what else is there?<br /> They probably couldn't, and might not have wanted to is what it boils down to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they probably did try, but were beaten back by the Dragonblooded and their Sidereal allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:42:21-07:00","id":1397693,"title":"","content":"Or they couldn't work up the heart to add more death to both sides. The Contagion and then the Balorian Crusade, so much death...and failure. Maybe they were reeling, maybe they went to lick their wounds figuring they could play the long game only to find the Sidereals played it better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T05:47:02-07:00","id":1397694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397690#post1397690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And they probably did try, but were beaten back by the Dragonblooded and their Sidereal allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was going to answer just this. If you want that they did, well they tried and most likely failed (or now you have to explain how they actually succeed and why is the Empress still in power ?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:11:07-07:00","id":1397698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397694#post1397694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was going to answer just this. If you want that they did, well they tried and most likely failed (or now you have to explain how they actually succeed and why is the Empress still in power ?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Big red is and always has been a lunar, she's just in disguise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:12:54-07:00","id":1397699,"title":"","content":"The Silver Pact isn't as unified as it pretends to be and your typical Lunar isn't fighting for Celestial Exalted hegemony but against whatever shit the Dragon-Blooded have done fairly recently.<br /> <br /> To an extent the elders may have had to allow the Realm to become the villain of a new age because if they'd attacked too soon younger Lunars might have had serious questions about whose side they were on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-20-2020, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:33:49-07:00","id":1397708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397698#post1397698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big red is and always has been a lunar, she's just in disguise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I totally can see the succeding Lunars going full &quot;Better to reign in Hell than serve in Heaven&quot; and reestablish their dreamed hegemony of the First Age. Suits me !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T06:45:09-07:00","id":1397712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397699#post1397699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Pact isn't as unified as it pretends to be and your typical Lunar isn't fighting for Celestial Exalted hegemony but against whatever shit the Dragon-Blooded have done fairly recently.<br /> <br /> To an extent the elders may have had to allow the Realm to become the villain of a new age because if they'd attacked too soon younger Lunars might have had serious questions about whose side they were on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, that kind of feels to me like one of those answers that just adds more complications than it resolves.<br /> <br /> Unless one is going for a story in which player Lunars become cynical about the intentions and rationality of their elders and seek to break away or reform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:14:42-07:00","id":1397722,"title":"","content":"This was the time when Raksi and Ma-Ha-Suchi went to war with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T07:19:23-07:00","id":1397723,"title":"","content":"I can\u2019t speak for dev intent, but my assumption is that Lunars try to infiltrate the Realm on the regular, and regularly fail outright or succeed to a lesser degree than snatching the biggest prize. I assume they did the same to the Shogunate. The Empress was a Shogunate soldier well-familiar with the risks Lunars would pose. The Wyld Hunt may not have been a Sidereal-backed religious institution at the time, but I\u2019m sure the Empress had something similar in place, even putting aside her personal security, the risk of horrifying reprisals with the Sword of Creation, and the possibility that the Fair Folk will resume their invasion if the Empress can\u2019t wipe them out any more.<br /> <br /> A Circle of Lunar PCs could\u2019ve overcome all that, and in your post-Contagion game, they can! The Time of Tumult presupposes that you didn\u2019t set a game at that point in history and disrupt the timeline with PC shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 06-20-2020, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:39:41-07:00","id":1397741,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that this whole question is premised on the idea that Lunars at the beginning of the Realm Era have all of the same knowledge of what's going on as Lunars at the end of that era do. But imagine actually being in the shoes of those people while events are ongoing.<br /> <br /> The world has just gone through a period of feeling as though it was going to end, with the widespread plague and accompanying shadowlands followed by the ravenous Fair Folk hordes and accompanying dissolution of reality, followed by the rains of fire and poison and iron thorns (which, in the moment, seems like it might feel more like another sign of the eschaton rather than salvation).<br /> <br /> You're a Lunar going through all of that, presumably one that has been fighting the Shogunate for a few decades or centuries, and have managed to survive these latest incomprehensibly vast ordeals.<br /> <br /> So what is going to stand out to you more:<br /> <br /> The gradual formation and consolidation of a new governing and military body laying groundwork for a system of world domination in the far distant Blessed Isle?<br /> <br /> Or the fact that all of the local Shogunate institutions have been completely smashed beyond recognition?<br /> <br /> If we assume that a Lunar in that period has <i>no reason to believe that heading to the Blessed Isle is an overriding priority</i>, then the idea that their first objective would be trying to fix things up where they are right now seems sensible enough. Where are they supposed to be getting the intelligence that the Blessed Isle is going to become an important target prior to the point that it becomes fortified enough that doing anything about it becomes commensurately difficult?<br /> <br /> The Bronze Tigers can be assumed to have the advantages of already being pretty embedded in the kind of structures that have necessitated the tactics of the Silver Pact in the first place, and they become a challenge to the Scarlet Empress because they're a lot closer and more openly belligerent. One might assume that the more experienced Lunars have long integrated a practice of not flexing at enemies whose strength has not yet been surmised.<br /> <br /> One might also assume that right now, the largest number of fresh Lunars is newly incarnating all at once since the Usurpation. Even assuming they <i>could</i> think that getting to the Blessed Isle right now is a priority, the portrayal of the Silver Pact makes it not unbelievable that getting through to as many young Lunars as possible rather than leaving them to their own devices is a higher concern.<br /> <br /> But it's all primarily revolving around the point that they don't have something to inform them that getting over to the Blessed Isle right now ought to be their biggest priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:43:58-07:00","id":1397742,"title":"","content":"I'd also like to think that Lunars used that time of Weakness for the Realm well, not by invading the center but by carving off vast chunks of the threshold free of the Realm's control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T08:51:57-07:00","id":1397747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397742#post1397742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to think that Lunars used that time of Weakness for the Realm well, not by invading the center but by carving off vast chunks of the threshold free of the Realm's control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think explanations need to be consistent with how the setting is portrayed. It depends on what you mean by vast chunks free of control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:02:33-07:00","id":1397749,"title":"","content":"I'm not up to date on Deeb history as of currently, does the Realm control all the territory the Shogunate used to rule? Is it larger?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:33:00-07:00","id":1397755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397742#post1397742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to think that Lunars used that time of Weakness for the Realm well, not by invading the center but by carving off vast chunks of the threshold free of the Realm's control.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually exactly what Leviathan did for the West as I gather, and to some extent what Ma-Ha-Suchi did in relation to the Dreaming Sea region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:34:48-07:00","id":1397756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397749#post1397749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not up to date on Deeb history as of currently, does the Realm control all the territory the Shogunate used to rule? Is it larger?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually not clear the Shogunate and Realm are isomorphic at all. The Terrestrial Shogunate seems to have had a very very weak hold on the Blessed Isle as a whole to my gathering and was based more in the East primarily, with I think consequences on how that affected its control/administration/etc. of the rest of the world. It might be my own biases, but I get a sense the currently politically unified Blessed Isle in 3e is in itself something fairly unique to the Scarlet Dynasty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T09:42:46-07:00","id":1397758,"title":"","content":"I think the realm is smaller, now that you mention it.<br /> <br /> At the very least, the shogunate stretched as far as Lookshy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-20-2020, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T10:07:21-07:00","id":1397761,"title":"","content":"The Shogunate is meant to essentially refer to the whole world as governed by the Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Just not governed by the Dragon Blooded well. The original portrayal had consistent difficulty keeping subject peoples in line, local daimyos would frequently hold out and fight amongst themselves, and the central government was subject to inconsistent power and frequent assassinations, coups and total collapse.<br /> <br /> The Realm is more centralised and effectively balances its factions, while exerting power beyond its borders with a more indirect method. Even within the range of satrapies, it definitely controls much less of the world.<br /> <br /> Still, the Lunars have not so much carved out much of the world for themselves as they often occupy key positions and engage in harassment and sabotage that ultimately limits how far the Realm's authority can extend. Ma-Ha-Suchi's chunk is small, but it's strategically placed to limit access to the Dreaming Sea, a zone that widely evolves devoid of direct Exalted influence.<br /> <br /> Still, that's probably more emergent than deliberate, when the Silver Pact emphasizes varied local strategies that keep the Realm off balance. There are plenty of Lunars who don't want to cut off parts of the world, they want to make those parts cripplingly expensive to govern and a source of constant internal tension. Better to make the Dynasts destroy one another over the question of who rules in Chiaroscuro than unite them around preventing you from ruling there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T10:33:58-07:00","id":1397763,"title":"","content":"I see it as the Shogunate notionally controlling most of Creation.<br /> <br /> Post Contagion, the Shogunate is gone. The Deebs are forced back to the Blessed Isle and consolidate there. The Lunars, principally, exist in the Threshold. New Lunars are Exalting in the wake of the apocalypse... and they want to rebuild their shattered homes. If they're young enough, they might not even know what a &quot;Shoguate&quot; or even a &quot;Dragon-Blooded&quot; is. Lunar elders are either squabbling with each other, like Ma-Ha and Raksi, or rebuilding their own homes, like Leviathan, or saying &quot;f-this, I'm an owl now&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some are going to strike directly at the Realm. But they're spread throughout a destroyed, post-Apocalyptic world. The Bronze Faction, itself divided by infighting, have few elements of the Vision of Bronze left to defend. The Realm has the Sword of Creation, greatest weapon in the Exalted aresnal to defend itself.<br /> <br /> In 2E, Dragon-Blooded and Lunars fought side-by-side against the Fair Folk. Perhaps furative envoys seek to turn &quot;ceasefire&quot; into &quot;peace&quot; during this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T10:56:50-07:00","id":1397767,"title":"","content":"Just as a slight correction since it's come up a couple of times, Luthe sinking and Leviathan retreating there happened at the start of the Shogunate, not the end of it, and he never fought against that government. It actually comes across that the city weathered the Contagion pretty well.<br /> <br /> That's the basis of Sha'a Oka's grudge against him; the Black Lion resents this ancient acclaimed war hero having sat it out in his fancy underwater city while the other Lunars fought for their lives and freedom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:21:34-07:00","id":1397770,"title":"","content":"It also seems like there were a lot of Shogunate successor states the Lunars could have been fighting, and it's not clear that, in RY 1, anyone could tell that this &quot;Scarlet Empress&quot; person was clearly the highest priority. They had evidence, but there were a lot of Dragonblooded carving out culturally Shogunate but politically distinct empires.<br /> Also, a bunch of these governments no longer exist, and while several got conquered/absorbed by the Realm, it's entirely possible that the explanation for what happened to the governments descended from Shogunate generals/regional governors/whatever is pretty frequently &quot;Lunars&quot;, and the Realm is the one that survived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T11:26:40-07:00","id":1397773,"title":"","content":"It's the end of the Contagion. Between the plague, the Fair Folk, the walking dead, rogue Shogunate forces, and people who've turned bandit to survive, Lunar A herself has experienced several nasty close calls, and almost all of the people she cares about have died. Most of her mortal family, friends, loyal retainers, and the like died, and the rest are are only hanging on with her aid.<br /> <br /> Lunar B shows up and says, &quot;Hey! I bet the Dragon-Blooded are on the ropes now too. Come with me and we'll try to finish them off! While you're gone, your friends will be helpless and they'll probably all die. Also, I know you want to live and all, but if you come with me, you may die. Also, if you die, your reincarnation won't give a shit about your friends, so they're even more likely to die. But hey, it's not like your life or your friends' lives are as important as this vendetta!&quot;<br /> <br /> It seems unlikely to me that Lunar A would necessarily support the proposition offered to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T12:50:12-07:00","id":1397792,"title":"","content":"In addition to the above it wouldn't really have helped. Let's go with a hypothetical of a group of a Lunars that were near enough by that they could have done anything, shits already rock bottom for them or seizing the area around what would be called the Imperial Manse would be a major boon to their goals of ensuring the survival of people important to them. And since we're not talking about a version of Reality where her Redness forged an alliance with a particular group of Lunars, they either don't talk to her or said talk is met by refusal combat and one thing leads to another and someone is dead. To continue the hypothetical let's say it was the Empress, great she's dead and unless the Sword answers to literally anyone holding the hearthstone and helpfully imparts all knowledge of functions they can't use the Sword to defend it when the Tigers show up or the messaging function Her Redness used to declare herself ruler of the world for whatever reason they wanted.<br /> <br /> Kejack and the other Sids probably aren't gonna be trying to help these Lunars consolidate power like they did with The Scarlet Empress in the main timeline, a lot of people are gonna be coming for the group's head because Anathema and I wouldn't be surprised if the information that they murdered the woman who saved the world to get her power got out as a potential rallying point for various other factions and the other Lunars are still probably not in a position that they would be able to signficantly help against this even if they didn't have stuff they were handling making sure their little parts of the world don't get listed as after the fact casualties of the contagion and rhaksha invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T13:02:39-07:00","id":1397794,"title":"","content":"chiming in -<br /> <br /> One of thing I like about the current edition of the setting, is that it positions the various factions as made up of individuals. Individuals with beliefs and goals, passionate emotions, and as prone to irrationality, limitations, and sometimes just plain bad luck as anyone. If there was a single hand guiding the Lunars, that had read the sourcebooks and knew the proper strategy to &quot;win&quot; the game, then I could see a Lunar takeover happening. Unfortunately, they were a scattered collection of individuals who had just suffered a unprecedented calamity and most likely had higher priorities than knocking off yet another DB that proclaimed themselves Queen of the World.<br /> <br /> And this (IMHO) feels far more organic and realistic, as it is closer to how people (even powerful ones) actually behave, and how events tend to actually unfold. For the most part, we can only tell when the world has changed in hindsight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-20-2020, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T15:41:06-07:00","id":1397835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397770#post1397770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also seems like there were a lot of Shogunate successor states the Lunars could have been fighting, and it's not clear that, in RY 1, anyone could tell that this &amp;quot;Scarlet Empress&amp;quot; person was clearly the highest priority. They had evidence, but there were a lot of Dragonblooded carving out culturally Shogunate but politically distinct empires.<br /> Also, a bunch of these governments no longer exist, and while several got conquered/absorbed by the Realm, it's entirely possible that the explanation for what happened to the governments descended from Shogunate generals/regional governors/whatever is pretty frequently &amp;quot;Lunars&amp;quot;, and the Realm is the one that survived.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can imagine several northern Lunars developing the idea that Bagrash Kol's empire represents a greater threat in its day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-20T20:32:52-07:00","id":1397888,"title":"","content":"Try to think like a Lunar Elder for a minute here. You're reeling, your armies are broken, the world is hectic and confused. There may be a second invasion at any moment. Why would you rush to kill a Dragon blood? Some Terrestrial captain set herself up as Empress on the Blessed Isle? Cool! Neat! She can knock herself out for what, how long do Dragon Bloods live? Two hundred years? Sweet! You can have an army of beastmen just in time to mop up the mess her inevitable death will leave as her children squabble over her throne.<br /> <br /> Actually, turns out they were right about that last one, just very wrong about the timetable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T04:12:15-07:00","id":1397945,"title":"","content":"I'm finding myself inclined not to go too far in the direction of Lunars being dismissive of the danger. That would not gel with what the driving purpose of the Silver Pact was, and the experience of its members. It's also plausible enough that there are Lunars in the correct place to hear the stories coming in of how the Blessed Isle is in a state of recovery, how its surviving daimyos and legions are clustering around the ancient manse, and then the news of images of a newly proclaimed monarch appearing all over it. Very ominous rumblings.<br /> <br /> But such a person is also plausibly alone at the time, and the things coming down the wire that make the nascent Realm sound worth attacking are also the kind of thing that make the prospect of attacking it alone seem unviable. That person needs to range around and try and figure out which Lunars are still alive and who can be rallied to try and do something about it first. The time taken to do that is time in which the Realm consolidates itself.<br /> <br /> But yes, there's also the way that reading between the lines of Fangs at the Gate conveys an impression of Lunars at the start of the Realm Era who were... sluggish. You've got older ones that have become weary of the fight, you've got a whole generation that Exalted during the Great Contagion who aren't really invested in struggles for dominion over Creation in the first place. This does contrast significantly with the kind of verve and energy that necessarily goes into the formation of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it is possible to read the inability of the Silver Pact to capitalise on that vulnerable moment and nip something that will prove very dangerous and challenging in the bud. That the moment was theirs and they lacked the initiative to seize it.<br /> <br /> That's okay. It's okay for key moments in the history of the setting to be driven by some group's failures or mistakes. The Exalted are not perfect, not tireless, not fully rational actors even without the interventions of the Great Curse. History as driven by the interplay of success and failure makes the setting more representative of reality.<br /> <br /> The assertion that one circle of Lunars could have held the entire Blessed Isle against all of the opposing Dragon Blooded residing there is still completely absurd, though.<br /> <br /> And pushing even beyond that... the establishment of the Realm is not an immediate thing to be sure, we're even informed in reasonable detail of the successive stages and the fact that it took decades to get truly up and running, but it does still come across as a thing driven by a distinct level of speed, energy, ambition and good decision making. It recalls to me things like the historical context of Napoleon or Alexander the Great; it wasn't just that those people were excellent tactical and strategic planners, it was the fact that they just kept <i>going at it</i>, that there was a determination there that does seem to be uncommon historically (it was certainly uncommon among their contemporaries). <br /> <br /> There's nothing in the nature of the setting that should mean that, in that particular moment, the personality for that kind of rapid mobility was possessed of a Terrestrial Exalt and lacking among the surviving Lunar Exalted (even if perhaps it was something that they'd had in the past and lost; Napoleon was ultimately defeated by his own aging as much as he was by the greater strategic concerns and growing tactical acumen of his opponents).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T06:22:57-07:00","id":1397973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397945#post1397945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing in the nature of the setting that should mean that, in that particular moment, the personality for that kind of rapid mobility was possessed of a Terrestrial Exalt and lacking among the surviving Lunar Exalted (even if perhaps it was something that they'd had in the past and lost; Napoleon was ultimately defeated by his own aging as much as he was by the greater strategic concerns and growing tactical acumen of his opponents).</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one thing sort of meaning that - there are were ... thousands? of dragon blooded, and probably well under 400 lunars. For any personality, you'd expect there to be several times as many dragon blooded than lunars with that personality.<br /> <br /> This also gets into one advantage each side has - There are way more Terrestrials than Lunars, and insofar as Terrestrials are united they will generally win through numbers, but it's much easier to organize 5 people than 25 or 250. &quot;Set up a bunch of small Dominions in the Threshold&quot; plays well to the Lunar strengths, since it encourages Dragonblooded to spend their time fighting each other instead of lunars, while &quot;Establish a huge Realm in the center of the world&quot; plays well to Dragonblooded strengths, since it sets up a single point to unify around.<br /> <br /> There's a weird stasis to this argument, where any time the Dragonblooded Realm is winning everyone starts trying to get a larger slice of the pie instead of expanding it so the growth stops, and once it starts losing everyone manages to pull themselves together to save themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T07:47:55-07:00","id":1397981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397945#post1397945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The assertion that one circle of Lunars could have held the entire Blessed Isle against all of the opposing Dragon Blooded residing there is still completely absurd, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically when we have these discussions it's a simulationist issue.<br /> The Lunar can probably get the jump on and kill a Dragon-Blooded before escaping retaliation because of clear mechanical advantages. The ability of other Dragon-Blooded to recognise that someone is picking them off one by one and adapt in response is mostly narrative so it gets discounted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T09:28:31-07:00","id":1397994,"title":"","content":"my best guess, they couldn't. Yes lunars are strong, but the great contagion was a plague that affected all beings. in addition, even if the lunars united there are only 300 of them and a few thousand barbarians, and those numbers are doubtlessly reduced by the contagion. the realm still has legions of dragon bloods. Then of course they get hit by the balorian crusade first because they lurk on the outskirts of creation. And to cap off the reasoning, the Scarlet Empress manages to use the sword of creation. that all adds up to the lunars being unable to press the advantage.<br /> <br /> of course, I know nothing about 3ed. I might be completely wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T14:50:16-07:00","id":1398066,"title":"","content":"sids would have organized hunts for any lunar that got to powerful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T22:34:19-07:00","id":1398125,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s some discussion of this in The Realm, specifically starting on page 15. Apparently the Scarlet Empress barely survived several Lunar assassins in the early days of the Realm and, between that and the meat grinder they tended to turn their lairs into, this was what led to her turning to the Immaculate Order and calling for a major Wyld Hunt initiative.<br /> <br /> I would tend to agree with the people in this thread that have asserted that the Lunars 1) had more urgent things to worry about at home and 2) either didn\u2019t know about the threat of the Realm or dismissed it as \u201cjust another petty DB kingdom.\u201d And then, once the Realm started flexing its might and the threat became clearer, the assassins started having very personal reasons to show up, like \u201cyou destroyed my village\u201d and off we go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T05:46:16-07:00","id":1398165,"title":"","content":"I feel as though a lot of this question is resolved by fully integrating the spirit of how Fangs at the Gates portrays the Lunar Exalted, in contrast with how a lot of people might have expected the Lunars to be portrayed for a variety of reasons.<br /> <br /> To put it simply, I think the original Lunars book was written heavily informed by a narrative of &quot;barbarian peoples&quot; who engage in violence for its own sake rather than for greater strategic concerns. That for better or worse, many people built up an image that even Third Edition Lunars would be deeply immersed in violence. And the Exalted Third Edition core book did indeed introduce the concept of Lunar Dominions in terms of them being this thing that Lunars continuously build up and expend upon the Realm for the purposes of its destruction in perpetuity.<br /> <br /> Fangs at the Gate ultimately depicts the Lunars as having more nuance and humanity, in parallel with the people that they're embedded with. There's an underlying awareness that the sole concern is not with the methods that must be employed to fight, but decisions on whether to fight at all and understanding of what exactly you're fighting for. The Silver Pact ultimately does not think its existence is compatible with that of the Realm (in addition to several points for consideration that regard the Realm's existence as less desirable than their own), but one might say that several Lunars are living as though they know that they can last for centuries and that to live in terms of &quot;all warfare all the time&quot; is not desirable or sustainable, so they can afford to spend periods of time in a manner indistinguishable from being reconciled to the existence of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Also for there to be strategic considerations by which they employ a greater variety of means for constantly seeking the Realm's end than direct warfare, whether that be soft power, undermining them spiritually or metaphysically, environmental degradation or cultivation of disease.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that in the origins of the Realm there was necessarily a deliberate reflection on &quot;this isn't the best moment to start a big fight on our part&quot;, but just to say that there's a general attitude to what they're after that would reasonably not be prioritizing the best way to bring a fight at all times.<br /> <br /> One might judge the Realm as the Scarlet Empress built it up to be a thing that does not know how to not fight. Sure, there seem to be a lot of instances and policies in which it is holding off on a specific fight (for purposes of conquest) until later, but the driving force of the culture of their ruling elite is one that is concerned with unambiguous domination; they can brook no equals and all lesser powers must ultimately submit. The Realm is not ultimately in a state of genuine peace with its less powerful neighbours, it just hasn't gotten around to conquering them yet. I feel that <i>The Realm</i> is consistent with this interpretation when it presents the ultimate purpose of the satrapies as being defensive; they view all the rest of the world as a source of hostility against which they need to constantly be on guard.<br /> <br /> If we measured this against historical example, it would not be a sustainable attitude. In the setting of Creation it might be seen as being lengthened beyond what might be expected, which could be logically backed up a bit by the supernatural potency of the people and resources behind it, but there's still an attitude in the current writing that is aware of the unsustainability of the Realm. That's before one gets to the point that the Realm props itself up on an unstable alliance of highly competitive and self-interested factions who were only ever balanced by the constant interventions of a very powerful monarch.<br /> <br /> It does become a bit of a chicken and the egg kind of situation if one wants to determine whether this highly unstable and violent system is the reason for or result of the Silver Pact, although it can probably be approached as both. Particularly if one is not concerned with the Lunars being entirely moral actors; that they could be the types that say &quot;the Realm's method and purpose of rule is inherently destructive, which we're going to demonstrate and exploit by constantly provoking them into continuing it until they lose all credibility and fall apart&quot;. But it does lead back to a point that the Realm is expending itself in defence against fangs at the gate, and thus it has been more in the interests of Lunars to be at the gate than at the throat; that there's greater value and less risk to have fed into the perception of the wider world being inherently hostile than to have surged right at the heart of the enemy and make themselves a clearly distinguished target.<br /> <br /> That and I'd judge the Realm's attitude as part of a continuum from the Shogunate's policies, which I see as emergent from a severe failing of the Sidereal Exalted (or at least how I'd like them to be portrayed going forwards). There's a lot that I want to say about what I think would be a good way to portray their motives and how that related to prophecy going forward, but for now I'll keep it to the point that I would judge the Sidereals as having fundamentally misunderstood exactly what made the Solars so dangerous. That they viewed things in terms of &quot;going mad with power is acceptable enough so long as you're not <i>too</i> powerful&quot; and so they opted to swap out the Solar Exalted for the Terrestrial on the reasoning that the latter would be easier to control and less damaging in their abuses when they came up.<br /> <br /> It isn't solely on them, but it's part of my idea that there should be a fundamental question of whether the Age of Sorrows is really meaningfully better than the future they were trying to avoid, and that either way the Time of Tumult represents a turning point at which everything is on the verge of coming to a collapse anyway, hence the return of the Solars. That's not even about threats from the Wyld or cthonic or infernal forces, which I would characterize a lot like Surtur in Ragnarok; by the time you roll over to incinerate everything, all that's left anyway is the ruins in the aftermath of all of the pride and distrust and spite finally turning in on itself (the fact of it doing so being the main reason that you're free to incinerate).<br /> <br /> (Lest this post feel like it's affording too much credit to the Lunars, I'll just say that while I view them as being in a somewhat better place than the Realm, their ultimate goals are still too focused on victory rather than reconciliation to absolve them for responsibility in the crisis faced by the game's world at the point where Solars return to it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T09:13:02-07:00","id":1398191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398165#post1398165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Lest this post feel like it's affording too much credit to the Lunars, I'll just say that while I view them as being in a somewhat better place than the Realm, their ultimate goals are still too focused on victory rather than reconciliation to absolve them for responsibility in the crisis faced by the game's world at the point where Solars return to it)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the culture of the Silver Pact is made more healthy in part than the Realm by how the two kinds of Exalts are Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact generally has to recruit adults with world-shaping powers who have never before interacted with the Silver Pact. It fundamentally has to present a culture enticing to people not in it. &quot;Rule over a culture you craft as you see fit, with the option to apprentice yourself under a more experienced person with similar capabilities to you, and engage in trade with powerful peers whose specialties differ from yours. Also, work together to try to stop the people who want to kill all of us from doing that&quot; is an ideology you can recruit people to much easier than &quot;Dedicate your life to gaining influence and power, only to throw it away in endless violence for the sake of violence&quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, most Dragonblooded are born into being Dragonblooded. They can be part of the culture from birth, to the extent that its failures seem like the default state of the world. They are raised to expect the world to be their enemy/their target to be subjugated, and would need to actively seek out a different culture in order to be part of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:13:58-07:00","id":1398202,"title":"","content":"Why didn't the anarchist furries opposed to imperialism immediately turn around and become imperialists, indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T11:57:43-07:00","id":1398212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398202#post1398202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why didn't the anarchist furries opposed to imperialism immediately turn around and become imperialists, indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Silver Pact on the whole is far from anarchist and not specifically anti-imperialist, even if particular members hold either of those positions. You also have ones that are rather contrary to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T04:08:57-07:00","id":1398322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398191#post1398191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the culture of the Silver Pact is made more healthy in part than the Realm by how the two kinds of Exalts are Exalted.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact generally has to recruit adults with world-shaping powers who have never before interacted with the Silver Pact. It fundamentally has to present a culture enticing to people not in it. &amp;quot;Rule over a culture you craft as you see fit, with the option to apprentice yourself under a more experienced person with similar capabilities to you, and engage in trade with powerful peers whose specialties differ from yours. Also, work together to try to stop the people who want to kill all of us from doing that&amp;quot; is an ideology you can recruit people to much easier than &amp;quot;Dedicate your life to gaining influence and power, only to throw it away in endless violence for the sake of violence&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, most Dragonblooded are born into being Dragonblooded. They can be part of the culture from birth, to the extent that its failures seem like the default state of the world. They are raised to expect the world to be their enemy/their target to be subjugated, and would need to actively seek out a different culture in order to be part of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that better? (Yes, but...)<br /> <br /> Consider, our young Lunar. Likely poorly educated, likely downtrodden. The criteria for Supreme Executive Power has been granted to them by a Glowing Bint handing out Exaltations. There's no &quot;consent of the governed&quot; here, unless that's the type of government the Lunar chooses.<br /> <br /> You've given someone the power of the gods and told them &quot;do as thou wilt&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's way more <i>desirable</i> than seven centuries of tradition, but the argument that it's healthier is unproven. (It <i>is</i>, but, like, not by much.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T04:36:46-07:00","id":1398328,"title":"","content":"My perspective is that Lunars have been in a position where there's an incentive for them to reassess perspectives on what the valid use of power is. Those who have made a game attempt at it are not all the way there yet, and there are cases where some have leaned deeply into their own bad elements, but there's an impetus there, which is more than core Dragon Blooded have had during their hegemony and more than the Solars had at their height.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T06:09:11-07:00","id":1398341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398328#post1398328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My perspective is that Lunars have been in a position where there's an incentive for them to reassess perspectives on what the valid use of power is. Those who have made a game attempt at it are not all the way there yet, and there are cases where some have leaned deeply into their own bad elements, but there's an impetus there, which is more than core Dragon Blooded have had during their hegemony and more than the Solars had at their height.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cautiously agree.<br /> <br /> Agree because what you've written makes sense.<br /> <br /> Cautiously because, well, look at the first three pages of this thread and I'm sure some fans would take this statement and infer that ONLY Lunar Exalted are capable of acting morally.<br /> <br /> The status quo has little pragmatic use for undermining its own power structure. But I do kinda feel like the average Lunar looks at the status quo and says &quot;the world is a mess... and I just need to rule it! *Maniacal Laugh*&quot;<br /> <br /> And I realize Fangs has done a lot to try and soften that blow. But I'm still cautious over the difference between &quot;these people's circumstances have afforded them oppertunities collectively, but individuals may buck the trend&quot; (valid, useful) and &quot;All Lunars are RIGHT. All Dragon-Blooded are WRONG.&quot; (neither morally valid nor useful in an RPG).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T09:24:38-07:00","id":1398373,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons why the Seven Tigers posed an existential threat to the early Realm is that they, arguably, had more of a legitimate &quot;right&quot; to consolidate and rule over the remnants of the Shogunate than the Empress did -- they were a group of high ranking generals, while she was a single low-ranking officer. Taking over and ruling the Dragon-Blooded Host post-Contagion required, to some extent, the consent of the Dragon-Blooded Host, and if the Seven Tigers had been successful at killing the Empress and seizing control of her power base -- or even just separating her from the Imperial Manse so she could no longer use it as her ace in the hole -- it would have made a powerful argument to anyone not wanting endless war (a lot of people, at that point) that everyone really ought to just recognize the Seven Tigers as the legit rulers so everyone can move on to living in a society again. Perceived legitimacy and the (at least grudging) consent of the governed is important when you're trying to seize control of the remnants of a decapitated state, which is what the Empress did. The Scarlet Empire is in large part built out of something that <i>started as</i> the Dragon Shogunate remnants, and the Empress spent centuries dismantling the gentes and constructing her Great Houses edifice in their place after she first seized power.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded Host would not have been collectively cool with a comparably sized Circle of Lunars doing the same thing, especially since, unlike the Seven Tigers, a hypothetical Circle of seven Lunars wouldn't have had the backing of huge Shogunate armies with Dragon-Blooded officer corps to lend them further legitimacy as leaders of the Dragon-Blooded Host. (Remember, the Seven Tigers weren't just seven guys. They were seven armed forces leaders with huge armed forces.)<br /> <br /> So, in a low-information environment where the Silver Pact is scattered and suffering huge casualties, no one knows what the hell is going on, everyone just died from a plague and then just died from elves and then also just died from fire and iron raining from the sky, it's really not surprising that no random group of seven Lunars decided &quot;Hey, if those seven generals with huge armies and a huge amount of perceived legitimacy could march on the center of the world and convince everyone of their ethnic group that they should be in charge just because they were really close to being in charge before, us seven rando furries could do it, too, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also everyone was probably more afraid of Bagrash K\u00f6l","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T16:50:52-07:00","id":1398463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398373#post1398373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dragon-Blooded Host would not have been collectively cool with a comparably sized Circle of Lunars doing the same thing, especially since, unlike the Seven Tigers, a hypothetical Circle of seven Lunars wouldn't have had the backing of huge Shogunate armies with Dragon-Blooded officer corps to lend them further legitimacy as leaders of the Dragon-Blooded Host. (Remember, the Seven Tigers weren't just seven guys. They were seven armed forces leaders with huge armed forces.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which can also be perceived in how the story of the Seven Tigers ended not with them being brought before the newly proclaimed Scarlet Empress, but vanishing (into a lye pit) en route, escorted by newly pledged servants of the Empress. There's a lot in the narrative of how the Realm started that involves pre-existing authorities independently deciding who to throw their lot in with, and making meaningful gestures to that effect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T17:25:09-07:00","id":1398468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397680#post1397680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I simply can't comprehend that why none of surviving Lunar staged a takeover like Seven Tigers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seven Tigers had an advantage no Lunar ever would, he was a dragon blooded and therefore someone the remnants of the shogunate might consider following if his faction gained prominence. But some filthy lunar anathema join together and cut the head off the nascent Scarlet Empire before it can cement its control and declares their wretched demonic coven rulers of the world? A bunch of the shogunates remnants are going to be banding together to challenge that notion hard core. Centuries of divergence and strife later Lookshy and the Realm are <i>still</i> willing to put aside their differences to get together and dogpile lunars on religious grounds for being far lesser of a threat then what you are suggesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T02:17:04-07:00","id":1398563,"title":"","content":"Perhaps they did try!<br /> <br /> How could anybody know, in the chaos of the post-contagion, how many of the Seven Tigers generals were indeed lunars in disguise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T12:36:43-07:00","id":1398635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398563#post1398563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they did try!<br /> <br /> How could anybody know, in the chaos of the post-contagion, how many of the Seven Tigers generals were indeed lunars in disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, for reasons stated upthread. And I think for general dramatic reasons of, especially in 3e, not tyring ot say everything which seemed importatn was Actually a Celestial in Disguise. I think also that the Seven Tigers appeared to have had enough trust and built up power base to be the Dragon-Blooded Daimyos they calimed to be, or enough that if it weren't the case it's meaningless since they got sky-lasered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T22:18:59-07:00","id":1398710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398563#post1398563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How could anybody know, in the chaos of the post-contagion, how many of the Seven Tigers generals were indeed lunars in disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might notice that the general\u2019s shadow seems to keep attempting to strangle the shadows of other Dragon-Blooded in his vicinity. <br /> <br /> Or that he doesn\u2019t cast a reflection. <br /> <br /> Or how his anima doesn\u2019t burn them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T00:28:52-07:00","id":1398727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398710#post1398710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might notice that the general\u2019s shadow seems to keep attempting to strangle the shadows of other Dragon-Blooded in his vicinity.<br /> <br /> Or that he doesn\u2019t cast a reflection.<br /> <br /> Or how his anima doesn\u2019t burn them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, DB anima flux won't burn other DBs, anyway. As for the rest:<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh that? It was due to the damn Fair Folk! You should know better manners than putting it in words, 'Purple Skin' Yashimoto! &quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T03:29:39-07:00","id":1398747,"title":"","content":"On the one hand: used sparingly , &quot;X is really Y in disguise&quot; can be a great source of drama.<br /> <br /> On the other: Terrestrial Exalted are Exalted. They're the elemental supersoliders who have ruled Creation for two thousand years. They're epic, mystically enlightened, larger than life heroes. You don't look at Superman and say &quot;Yeah, but The Presence is stronger, so when Supes beats up Solomon Grundy, that was really The Presence in disguise&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the question is &quot;why didn't Y do Z?&quot; then the answer of &quot;Because thousands of Exalted would have stopped them&quot; should be sufficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T04:48:53-07:00","id":1398752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1397661#post1397661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coordinated Lunar assault can easily break such opposition and occupy the ground. Though admittedly Bronze Faction intervention remains a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure can.<br /> As a matter of fact, it did! There are lunar holdings that openly defy the Realm, even today.<br /> <br /> Why would you think a scattered lunar host would fare better than this against an organized, if wounded, power that <i>has beaten them on better days</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 06-25-2020, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:15:31-07:00","id":1398798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398747#post1398747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand: used sparingly , &quot;X is really Y in disguise&quot; can be a great source of drama.<br /> <br /> On the other: Terrestrial Exalted are Exalted. They're the elemental supersoliders who have ruled Creation for two thousand years. They're epic, mystically enlightened, larger than life heroes. You don't look at Superman and say &quot;Yeah, but The Presence is stronger, so when Supes beats up Solomon Grundy, that was really The Presence in disguise&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the question is &quot;why didn't Y do Z?&quot; then the answer of &quot;Because thousands of Exalted would have stopped them&quot; should be sufficient.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that if there was a time to go for opportunistic action, the post-contagion would be it. Lunars are powers on themselves as individuals, DBs are much more dependent on organization. It is unlikely that some lunar would not jump on the opportunity (as, you know, the Empress did). Of course, they did not succeed, but this is beside the point. There should be lots of stories to be told about the epoch.<br /> <br /> If we are talking about defeatism, it only got worse from then on. In the current Realm year, there are more DBs than right after armageddon, and they are more organized (even with the civil war). Why is it applicable to say that 'Nothing can be done because thousands of DBs will stop you!' then, and not now? I would say that either way, it wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:48:27-07:00","id":1398807,"title":"","content":"This conversation is maddening even from the sidelines. It makes me think that the central, initial question of this thread isn\u2019t really a question but rather a veiled position for debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:11:39-07:00","id":1398825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398798#post1398798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that if there was a time to go for opportunistic action, the post-contagion would be it. Lunars are powers on themselves as individuals, DBs are much more dependent on organization. It is unlikely that some lunar would not jump on the opportunity (as, you know, the Empress did). Of course, they did not succeed, but this is beside the point. There should be lots of stories to be told about the epoch.<br /> <br /> If we are talking about defeatism, it only got worse from then on. In the current Realm year, there are more DBs than right after armageddon, and they are more organized (even with the civil war). Why is it applicable to say that 'Nothing can be done because thousands of DBs will stop you!' then, and not now? I would say that either way, it wouldn't be.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Phrasing.<br /> <br /> Why DIDN'T something happen? The Exalted.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean something COULDN'T happen in the future.<br /> <br /> Saying the Western dark age happened because of the Fall of Rome, does not mean that the Renaissance can never happen.<br /> <br /> If you want to tell stories about the early Lunar assaults on the Realm, I agree with you -- there are probably lots of them.<br /> <br /> But they didn't fail because the Empress is really a Solar in disguise. They failed because the Dragon-Blooded are amazingly powerful demi-gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:02:56-07:00","id":1398839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398798#post1398798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that if there was a time to go for opportunistic action, the post-contagion would be it. Lunars are powers on themselves as individuals, DBs are much more dependent on organization. It is unlikely that some lunar would not jump on the opportunity (as, you know, the Empress did). Of course, they did not succeed, but this is beside the point. There should be lots of stories to be told about the epoch.<br /> <br /> If we are talking about defeatism, it only got worse from then on. In the current Realm year, there are more DBs than right after armageddon, and they are more organized (even with the civil war). Why is it applicable to say that 'Nothing can be done because thousands of DBs will stop you!' then, and not now? I would say that either way, it wouldn't be.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So something to remember is that despite the Empress' use of the Sword of Creation, what &quot;taking a move&quot; even was is not clear. At the early days, the Blessed Isle had at least two polities (the Empress' Realm, Arjuf) and maybe a few more. You had Lookshy and Grand Cherak poised to rival them. And there might ahve been two or three other polities scattered about that Lunars <i>did</i> smash into bits, or which evnetually went sideways and weird like the Cult of the Violet Fang. So it might have just as much been &quot;Do what exactly?&quot;, along with other issues like what SLS noted with how folks are just picking pu pieces, the Shogunate the Silver Pact had been fighting for centuries to this point <i>was more or less defeated already</i>, and non-DB shit like Bagrash Kol was showing up.<br /> <br /> I honeslty am also not sure what winning or trying to take out the early Empress achieves that doing the same to Lookshy, Arjuf, or Cherak would have not been similarly the case. Besides the Sword, she actuallys eemed to kind of be the least likely to win IMHO (no real city base, less Shoguante infrastructure in tact ect.) It wouldnt' be at least a cnetury I think before folks realized she was the Big Deal and by then it was probably already too late. And even then, folks actually did try anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T03:19:30-07:00","id":1398995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398798#post1398798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should be lots of stories to be told about the epoch.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> I think it's fine for people to talk about an earlier phase of the setting as a place in which they might want to set a game, but I find myself doubting that this is really an intended (or at least prioritized) element of the gameplay, and hence the backstory is not particularly written to accommodate it. In which case, no, there shouldn't be lots of stories to tell; tell the one that matters and then move on. There's plenty of time between Realm Year 0 and game year 0 in which to give Lunars their due and they've gotten it, it is not necessary to put them absolutely everywhere.<br /> <br /> The story of the Realm's founding is perfectly cromulent even if Lunars are absent from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">there are more DBs than right after armageddon, and they are more organized (even with the civil war).</div> </div> </div> </div>They really aren't. The origin story for the Realm has always included just about every Dragon Blood of the Blessed Isle, including those in the (still professionally organised) military apparatus, pledging themselves to the new authority figure pretty quickly. They even put up with undignified procedures to be able to get personal audiences with her. The biggest discord apparently came from one petitioner being a bit patronising and presumptuous, before changing tack right quickly when the Empress chided him. It would seem that everybody prioritized harmony in a time of such extreme crisis.<br /> <br /> The current Realm is very much one in which the Houses are in fierce opposition to one another, ready to pull one another down to prevent them from rising to a greater position, and with several internal fracture points of divided loyalties and hidden agendas, having also recently compromised the efficiency of their military by not only dividing its strength under ten different organisers but gutted its meritocratic officer class in favour of appointments based on family loyalties.<br /> <br /> They're also written as not taking the Lunars that seriously. One can presume that the Shogunate was a lot more dedicated to fighting the Lunars and sussing out its threat within their own ranks, given descriptions of what the likes of Raksi were doing, which is also an environment in which effective infiltration is presumably more challenging. The way the Realm is written in Third Edition, they find an equilibrium of &quot;don't attack the heartland of the Realm hard enough to make a lot of them more concerned with coming back down on us&quot;. The Realm is supposed to have been a lot stronger in the past (even if never having the military power of the Shogunate, it was more internally stable, had sustained policies and a well fortified central point of control), and Lunar policies were already effectively weakening it. The Time of Tumult represents what might be an unexpected boon to provide an opportunity to defeat that weaker Realm in detail.<br /> <br /> (It may also represent possibilities that I imagine to have been a concern of several leading Lunars that had them argue against continuing to try and assassinate the Scarlet Empress)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398825#post1398825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Saying the Western dark age happened because of the Fall of Rome, does not mean that the Renaissance can never happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly helps that modern historography doesn't really consider the dark age to have been a thing anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are references now to a Frankish Renaissance. Architecture, agriculture and metallurgy continued to incrementally improve between the end of the Western Roman Empire and whatever starting point one might give to the Renaissance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 06-26-2020, 06:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:04:46-07:00","id":1399043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398995#post1398995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The story of the Realm's founding is perfectly cromulent even if Lunars are absent from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As established though, Lunars aren't absent from it. Lunar attempts on the life of the Empress are enshrined in 3E canon.<br /> <br /> You are correct that this isn't the default or intended time period to play in. But certainly there are dozens of stories which <i>could</i> be told in this time period.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398995#post1398995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly helps that modern historography doesn't really consider the dark age to have been a thing anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are references now to a Frankish Renaissance. Architecture, agriculture and metallurgy continued to incrementally improve between the end of the Western Roman Empire and whatever starting point one might give to the Renaissance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying Apollo 1 <i>did</i> fail because of a cabin fire doesn't mean Apollo 11 <i>couldn't</i> succeed.<br /> <br /> It's not incredulous that a fire which kills the entire crew might stop a space mission, as it is not incredulous that an empire of superpowered, mystic warriors wielding the power of the elements might prove victorious over magical shapeshifters empowered by the moon.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say the shapeshifters can't win, or couldn't have won, or that they won't eventually win thanks in part to learning from their mistakes, or seeking incremental victory. Merely that they didn't win, and this should not strain credulity.<br /> <br /> Just as it shouldn't strain credulity that the Divine Revolution was successful, nor the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> The Exalted are powerful. Dragon-Blooded are Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:23:40-07:00","id":1399046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398563#post1398563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps they did try!<br /> <br /> How could anybody know, in the chaos of the post-contagion, how many of the Seven Tigers generals were indeed lunars in disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way this has phrased makes me imagine a Lunar killing one of the Seven Tigers only to discover that another Lunar infiltrator had beaten them to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T06:51:20-07:00","id":1399053,"title":"","content":"IMO, having the Seven Tigers be Lunars takes a bit of narrative gravity out of the situation. They're supposed to be the last gasp of the anarchic warlordism that defined the Shogunate. The Empress defeating them symbolizes her defeat of the old de facto order where the Dragonblooded openly fought one another for shortsighted temporal power. Lookshy's grievance with the Empress has to do with chain of command and adherence to the de jure ideals of the Shogunate. The Seven Tigers' issue with the Empress is largely &quot;We have bigger armies and we want the power she has,&quot; which is largely what the Shogunate was underneath its ideals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","user":"HamSandLich","date":". 06-26-2020, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T07:16:34-07:00","id":1399059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399053#post1399053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, having the Seven Tigers be Lunars takes a bit of narrative gravity out of the situation. They're supposed to be the last gasp of the anarchic warlordism that defined the Shogunate. The Empress defeating them symbolizes her defeat of the old de facto order where the Dragonblooded openly fought one another for shortsighted temporal power. Lookshy's grievance with the Empress has to do with chain of command and adherence to the de jure ideals of the Shogunate. The Seven Tigers' issue with the Empress is largely &quot;We have bigger armies and we want the power she has,&quot; which is largely what the Shogunate was underneath its ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that having one of the Seven Tigers be a Lunar in disguise doesn't really diminish this, but any more than that would not be a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:07:24-07:00","id":1399079,"title":"","content":"&quot;How did we miss this? He's <i>literally a tiger</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:26:56-07:00","id":1399085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399046#post1399046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way this has phrased makes me imagine a Lunar killing one of the Seven Tigers only to discover that another Lunar infiltrator had beaten them to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399059#post1399059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that having one of the Seven Tigers be a Lunar in disguise doesn't really diminish this, but any more than that would not be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm enjoying the thought of combining these - of saying that there were many successful attempts to kill and replace members of the Seven Tigers - except they were all the same Tiger, as each Lunar killed and replaced another lunar without realizing it.<br /> <br /> The other six tigers have no idea this is going on, and none of the Lunars last long enough to pull off any plot before the Empress Sword of Creations them.<br /> <br /> This probably isn't the best interpretation for the sake of the setting, but on its own it's amusing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:50:43-07:00","id":1399089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399085#post1399085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm enjoying the thought of combining these - of saying that there were many successful attempts to kill and replace members of the Seven Tigers - except they were all the same Tiger, as each Lunar killed and replaced another lunar without realizing it.<br /> <br /> The other six tigers have no idea this is going on, and none of the Lunars last long enough to pull off any plot before the Empress Sword of Creations them.<br /> <br /> This probably isn't the best interpretation for the sake of the setting, but on its own it's amusing me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, the last Tiger who got sworded must have had SO MANY SHAPES. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Well this is weird, since I sacred hunted that Tiger I can now turn into a bat, a wolf, 17 different kinds of birds and fish, most known species of rodents, vermin and household pets, a few dinosaurs, and two dozen different people I've never seen before...</i>&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T09:54:37-07:00","id":1399090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399046#post1399046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way this has phrased makes me imagine a Lunar killing one of the Seven Tigers only to discover that another Lunar infiltrator had beaten them to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This always comes to mind:<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=825\" data-tempid=\"temp_825_1593189768880_623\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:18:40-07:00","id":1399101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1398825#post1398825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Phrasing.<br /> <br /> Why DIDN'T something happen? The Exalted.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean something COULDN'T happen in the future.<br /> <br /> Saying the Western dark age happened because of the Fall of Rome, does not mean that the Renaissance can never happen.<br /> <br /> If you want to tell stories about the early Lunar assaults on the Realm, I agree with you -- there are probably lots of them.<br /> <br /> But they didn't fail because the Empress is really a Solar in disguise. They failed because the Dragon-Blooded are amazingly powerful demi-gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is never just one cause for something, this is something historians say to sell books. The Dragon-Blooded are powerful demi-gods, but they were in a catastrophic time. They were depleted, disorganized, and divided. The dice could have gone either way, even more so without the hindsight of history. Assume that the decentralized organization of the Pact is also a guarantee that they can be fast and flexible when an opportunity arises, and they are more likely to cover all the bases.<br /> <br /> I never said that the Seven Tigers happened because of lunars. It's just that it is very unlikely that they did not have any involvement in this. Imagine what a coup would be if just one of the Seven Tigers was a deep-cover Lunar, and the Seven Tigers manage to take over creation! All that information and a huge powerbase! Bonus points if he could later incite a civil war to happen and make the Host deplete all their irreplaceable artifacts by killing themselves!<br /> <br /> Well, since they are all dead now, we will never know. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T11:56:34-07:00","id":1399108,"title":"","content":"It seems there is a general agreement that most important historical events in Exalted were not inevitable, and really could have gone either way. I am in complete agreement with this, as it seems to be a better story overall, in particular for a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there are any historical events in Exalted that were not inevitable.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was inevitable that the glories of the high First Age would someday end, although it could have ended in a number of vastly different ways than it did. Although maybe it was not inevitable in the sense that, by cooperating more than they compete and resisting the worst excesses of the Great Curse, the Exalted would always have the chance to keep it going for 10 more years and would keep getting those chances eternally until they failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:44:53-07:00","id":1399254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399090#post1399090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This always comes to mind:<br /> <br /> [ATTACH=CONFIG]temp_825_1593189768880_623[/ATTACH]</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean this?<br /> <img src=\"https://leadershipspirit.files.wordpress.com/2013/10/kingshaped.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:22:56-07:00","id":1399264,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> \ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02\ud83d\ude02","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T10:12:42-07:00","id":1399311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1397652-why-the-lunars-didn-t-take-over-the-realm-after-the-contagion?p=1399254#post1399254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly, thanks! Ah, what I posted appeared for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}